# Project overview

Production-ready **Next.js App Router** boilerplate (Next.js 16+, React 19, TypeScript **strict**).

## Stack (do not swap without explicit user request)

| Concern | Library |
|---------|---------|
| UI | Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui, Radix UI, Lucide |
| i18n | next-intl (`vi` default, `en`) |
| Client state | Zustand + `persist` middleware |
| Client fetch | SWR (via `/api/proxy`) |
| Forms | React Hook Form + Zod (`@hookform/resolvers`) |
| Theme / toast | next-themes, Sonner |
| HTTP (client) | Axios → `src/lib/axios-client.ts` only |

## Directory layout (`src/`)

- `app/[locale]/` — locale-scoped routes; route groups `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`
- `app/api/` — `proxy/[...path]`, `auth/*` (never expose `API_BASE_URL` to browser)
- `features/<domain>/` — actions, domain components (auth, product, user, dashboard)
- `components/{ui,common,layout,forms}/`
- `i18n/` — `routing.ts`, `request.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `messages/*.json`
- `stores/`, `swr/`, `hooks/`, `apis/`, `services/`, `lib/`, `types/`
- `proxy.ts` — locale routing + auth guard (Next.js 16; not `middleware.ts`)

## Next.js docs

This repo may differ from training data. Before changing routing, caching, or proxy/middleware APIs, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and heed deprecations (e.g. `proxy` vs `middleware`).

## Code style

- Minimal diff; match existing patterns; no drive-by refactors
- Path alias: `@/*` → `src/*`
- Run `npm run typecheck` after non-trivial TS changes
- Do not commit `.env.local` or secrets; keep `.env.example` in sync
